This document describes overlays provided in the kernel packages
For generic Armbian overlays documentation please see
https://docs.armbian.com/Hardware_Allwinner_overlays/

### Platform:

sun50i-h616 (Allwinner H616)

### Platform details:

Supported pin banks: PB, PC, PD, PH

Both SPI controllers have only one hardware CS pin exposed,
adding fixed software (GPIO) chip selects is possible with a separate overlay

I2C controller 2 (PE14, PE15) pins are used for non-I2C CSI functions or are not available
on supported boards, so this controller is not supported in provided overlays

### Provided overlays:

- spi-spidev
- spidev0_0
- spidev1_0
- spidev1_1
- spidev1_2
- i2c0
- ir
- tft35_spi
- tft35_spi25
- mcp2515
- pwm
- disable_uart0
- ws2812
- light

### Overlay details:

### spi-spidev

Activates SPIdev device node (/dev/spidevX.Y) for userspace SPI access,
where X is the bus number and Y is the CS number

SPI 0 pins (MOSI, MISO, SCK, CS): PC2, PC4, PC0, PC3
SPI 1 pins (MOSI, MISO, SCK, CS): PH7, PH8, PH6, PH5

Parameters:

param_spidev_spi_bus (int)
	SPI bus to activate SPIdev support on
	Required
	Supported values: 0, 1

param_spidev_spi_cs (int)
	SPI chip select number
	Optional
	Default: 0
	Supported values: 0, 1
	Using chip select 1 requires using "spi-add-cs1" overlay

param_spidev_max_freq (int)
	Maximum SPIdev frequency
	Optional
	Default: 1000000
	Range: 3000 - 100000000

### spidev0_0

Activates spi0 with cs0

SPI0 CS0 pins (MOSI, MISO, SCK, CS): PC2, PC4, PC0, PC3

### spidev1_0, spidev1_1, spidev1_2

Activates spi1 with cs0, cs1, cs2

SPI1 pins (MOSI, MISO, SCK): PH7, PH8, PH6
CS pins (0, 1, 2):
  CB1-SD: PC11, PC7, PC13
  CB1-eMMC: PI5, PI14, PI7

### i2c0

Activates TWI/I2C bus 0

I2C0 pins (SCL, SDA): PI5, PI6

### ir

Activates IR (Infrared remote) receiver

IR pin: PH10

### tft35_spi, tft35_spi25

Activates TFT35 (st7796s) screen

SPI pins: spidev1_1
DC pin:
  CB1-SD: PC14
  CB1-eMMC: PI15
I2C_GPIO pins (SCL, SDA):
  CB1-SD: PC10, PC12
  CB1-eMMC: PI4, PI6

### mcp2515

Activates MCP2515 (spi to can)

SPI pins: spidev1_0
IRQ pin:
  CB1-SD: PC9
  CB1-eMMC: PI3

### pwm

Activates PWM

### disable_uart0

Disable UART0 console output, these pins can be used for other features

### ws2812

Activates ws2812 RGB

pin:
  CB1-SD: PC14
  CB1-eMMC: PI15

### light

Activates light sensor for BIGTREETECH Pad7.
Enable 'i2c_gpio' and 'pwm', disable 'uart0'.

I2C_GPIO pins (SCL, SDA):
  CB1-SD: PC10, PC12
  CB1-eMMC: PI4, PI6
